  "culturalNote": "The Roman family (familia) was the foundation of society. The paterfamilias had absolute authority over his household. Terms like pater, mater, frater, and soror remain recognizable in Romance languages today.",
  "readingPassage": {
    "latin": "Rex Romanus populum regit. Milites ducis fortes sunt. Pater et mater liberos amant. Fratres et sorores in villa habitant. Nomen regis clarum est.",
    "translation": "The Roman king rules the people. The soldiers of the general are brave. The father and mother love their children. The brothers and sisters live in the villa. The name of the king is famous.",
    "notes": [
      "populus: people, nation",
      "fortis: brave, strong",
      "liberi: children (literally 'free ones')",
      "clarus: famous, clear"
    ]
